Source package: localsearch

Keeps the metadata extractor from crashing on a file which vanished between being queued and
being extracted, as the temporary files of a download do. The extractor aborted with
"free(): invalid pointer", see https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/localsearch/-/merge_requests/707,
which proposes both changes upstream. The other half of the fix is in patches/tinysparql/.

extractor-check-resource-before-printing.patch
    The crash fix, the first commit of the merge request. When committing an extraction result
    fails, the decorator retries the items one by one and, for an item which fails again,
    prints its metadata as SPARQL for the error report. An item without metadata has no
    resource, and printing the NULL resource crashed.

extractor-ps-fail-unreadable-file.patch
    The second commit of the merge request. The PS extractor reported a file it could not open
    as a success without metadata, so a vanished file reached the code above. It now fails
    with the error from opening the file, so the file is handled as a failed extraction.

extractor-ps-fail-unreadable-file-tests.patch
    A test for the PS extractor patch, not part of the merge request. It runs the extractor on
    a file which does not exist, with the MIME type given on the command line. The test is in
    the extractor suite because debian/rules ignores failures of the functional suite.

The decorator patch has no test. The crash needs a file to vanish after its extraction and
before the result is committed, which the test suite cannot arrange without depending on timing.
Either the decorator patch or the tinysparql patch alone prevents this crash.

Drop all three patches once Ubuntu ships a version which includes the merge request. If upstream
changed the commits before merging them, compare the merged code with the patches first. The
code they change is retry_synchronously in src/extractor/tracker-decorator.c and extract_ps,
extract_ps_gz and tracker_extract_get_metadata in src/extractor/tracker-extract-ps.c.

With the PS patch, a vanished PS file goes through tracker_decorator_info_complete_error, like a
failed extraction of any other kind. Ubuntu bug 2168518 reports a crash on that path with
localsearch 3.11.2 and glib 2.90, from Ubuntu 26.10. On 26.04 the path works, but after an
upgrade check that the bug is fixed before keeping the PS patch.
